preConditionHook:
// Weekly loss limit: off for the rest of the week once the week's equity
// change falls below -X. MonthlyProfitTarget is the reference for the shape, statement for
// statement: equity = NetProfit + OpenPositionProfit (close-marked, net of the
// entry side's costs), snapshotted as the PRIOR bar's equity on the first bar
// of each new week. PrevPeriod/PrevEquity mirror the twin's
// CurrentPeriod[1]/CurrentEquity[1] -- an EL variable's own history, 0 before
// the strategy's first evaluated bar -- advanced in endOfFileHook so the value
// read here is always the previous bar's.
//
// PERIOD: a new week starts on the first bar whose DayOfWeek(Date) is LOWER
// than the previous bar's (0 = Sunday .. 6 = Saturday, wall-clock close
// date, EL_Date_Probe.txt). A holiday Monday is absorbed (Fri -> Tue still
// decreases); Sunday-evening bars (@HO 18:00 open) start the week. Blind
// spot, identical in both twins: a data hole of 7+ days that resumes on a
// later weekday is not seen as a new week.
//
// LATCH CHECK: once the week's loss passes X the Switch forces flat and blocks entries, so
// equity stops moving; the next week boundary re-snapshots the start
// equity, the difference returns to 0, and trading resumes. It cannot disable
// the strategy for good. Direction-agnostic: both sides are identical text.
CurrentEquity = ctx.NetProfit() + ctx.OpenPositionProfit();
CurrentPeriod = day_of_week(day_of(ctx.Time(0)));
if (el_lt(CurrentPeriod, PrevPeriod)) {
    WeekStartEquity = PrevEquity;
}
